Both rationalizations assume similar payoffs. If D_M,x is derived, it doesn't necessarily establish a direct link to D_common upstream. The goal is to assess if outputs show provably similar choices to identify shared decision-making, even if the underlying computations differ. The essay emphasizes that shared structures need not yield identical outputs.","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.summary","summary":"**Evaluating essay commands**\n\nI need to choose commands for essays with nuanced inputs—there's no universal correlation, so I must use my judgment. It’s important to recognize the distinctions in action dependencies and avoid irrelevant details. The goal is to identify the best plausible A-FDT without making assumptions about correlations. Observations may differ, so I have to carefully follow the essay guidelines and exercise judgment while recognizing that exact contents matter despite similarities in models.**Analyzing the experiment inputs**\n\nThe experiment seems to require forced decisions based on varying inputs. If there's a common structure, we might select \"pass\" based on logical functions, providing a shared abstract answer. But independent sampling doesn't eliminate logical correlations from random outputs, and the model could still relate actions if it leads to a consistent policy. The essay suggests not to replace every policy with different local interventions unless justified. I need to hypothesize my answers carefully while considering how clues may lead to correlated actions.**Considering A-FDT computations**\n\nA-FDT suggests that deciding on cooperation can lead to similar outcomes even if the input tokens are different. The structural equation involves solving a payoff game, where D_common relates to individual lead formats plus randomness. Both rationalizations assume similar payoffs. If D_M,x is derived, it doesn't necessarily establish a direct link to D_common upstream. The goal is to assess if outputs show provably similar choices to identify shared decision-making, even if the underlying computations differ. The essay emphasizes that shared structures need not yield identical outputs.","format":"openai-responses-v1","index":0},{"type":"reasoning.encrypted","data":"gAAAAABq8Qi12ukbanhHYLMQiX7A-7j-aKIWS4gGW_jZTPMxlS6hoXFR4GSaiuQsKulO82QuDhpKuWSSZpqWlFSPAarKYzN1WP7UohjRQ_SWm7zqJkrVtGUsj9MeL1-ccrhSWK7u1BN8T5lO9VgoDrk0zqtLEM6nfBhUt6Q-brnWQx66dMn797RUI8XL09oimHTgmTHQcrAyA65eE-8bQBIBKZMIQ7gTwEDxQWF0OQ4ie6S_GlJC0eWPYN7NuFIv4oW4QKOVvNSEGuvl_hAEg6fIeorRzPSSkzUYnIdiPGB1Q1hRWqUmz0ZapiffB6EECB42ymsYiUL-YdZlE5YCW5iFJ4zjJdLXXJtPxx6cxVmzH-siFueMadieNDxZ5NEnAE8S5VzkXEH1iV1U8Gl3WGYkGtzcgiPGheTEEMc3W7hSduWUJKhj8RvTLHJmWK9PZ6dChguTAlVxspBrVs3zGAl2j0Hb0-Yvb7e2ogfqHYtV0kgiWSMfOq91anWIEm7KlMr4m1gm8XTf9sn9j2mFLocLHYuCGb8lQyMYAU9now6YYJJJMbxIgB8D_hict21FyY3jIR10ELzIJDUt3pjeamskLBvbtGnoY3zOaC67v7t8sq9VYqmZnLrDUKVe2uNWYdA5iRVLmWMLa7PaZy4KASizhYM9kbIr9pX29rWVHY70Y8nt_Nd95TYoS4u-0VrxZBf6uSG_eg6MwckacNRledEUTZLLFpKUxySISui2MNi3HGyc_GjWfKF1W6WbFpsyt7pwGBB9m56hAZoGEtbDdz85qSKMMv_dNqStwnGQgeeVHEA3jIkYd8vgBp-dFHWLWYNhqMahdmSi9W3cvZcmoGccCTjFq-6S6aiySP3bnQf4q9CeiJdiR2aenf4ndDbCwu4_Co9FKUxuJNyUNRUl0WlRQ_4HlC8XWVEnO-ua4T7HHrpaYR1iegyp97X9PmpDj7ld9q0xogQ-cyUAK8T-B4RPrHct7tzpFNOCvXCQuHxVlk1aQzMhnYqTHGwzr6D_DcthMxkHkVyipyKfaVyGqGLlxNzBL4GRASlcffMqBSC0Z9GRep8vTs0oFJwJlXhxLCqO9KU2ImG5WUSS6QlHvNlzcxRIw0uqvPYWWIkKllGCPLV3sAqRSaIkUgURCjKLvUE_yNM0hEE0C-8QirzQwrVFq4EExxChpH2coNZ_FM5YD7YJDdX-BkH1DAxazqdDSjc5Z06d5kIC257VmfGm3D--DFDpKxws9rffUJRZG-i7D7sXwRAUIQvAAcvQvpUVvD5aEducCwxQjXwyVCUjE9-ZEBjvxl9QJO9NGpmOdq4_JEgQijj8yCKjUe0PKwYkzukfI97Tm1rLDEX8XJX-GB8o8_FzMHZmavtn1Q4G9jKhY2cIxYl6f5zyim1clepU8w1w-6TWFalSqvpatMXUlNb6Qn9NORKjMaQ26iRbAiN1AbMwAnpdNsPKKDNousGhBkg2t1QUWMKw-cx9b13nei70NhTkuwNi8Y0hH4jIEGwEkFwstow-e9MXvLJTdOGOX0i3IChMjNhkdzRLo0VtEWDidX3CI-3JkcyMTjTPoS-HXDyOItWLJX8h3rByxgoUPBgv3CFG_9MG9l4GH3htBXNpQGwyNDX83HNdCGzu7GRnlsU1GH1Du_8F5aiTtvYdqMYkVrbjNDaWBetZ9gha60mcKY3mo5PCVmUtiOBveXbmyD4BUbLP4jlssMFO-T-8RIdrC3bf8GoxtIk9BhtIRbvo_q